# Cloudflare headers (honored by both Pages and Workers static assets).
#
# Cross-origin isolation for the apps that run the Kiln Python kernel. Kiln's
# Worker hard-requires SharedArrayBuffer (sys/kiln/worker-runtime.mjs), which the
# browser only exposes when the document is crossOriginIsolated — i.e. served
# with COOP: same-origin + COEP. We use `credentialless` so cross-origin
# subresources (Pyodide wasm/wheels from the CDN) load without a CORP header.
#
# Scope: /apps/forge/* and /apps/anvil/* (both run the Kiln kernel). As a
# TOP-LEVEL tab each isolates itself and `python` works; as an EMBEDDED iframe
# (Immersive) it is not isolated (the parent shell has no COOP/COEP) and degrades
# gracefully to the "needs cross-origin isolation" notice — no change to how the
# shell or any other embedded app loads. Isolating the shell itself is a
# separate, larger step (COI Phase 2).
# COI Phase 2 (host isolation) was attempted here and REVERTED 2026-08-26: putting
# COEP on the root blocked every cross-origin embedded app (MoD failed to load —
# transferSize 0, contentDocument null). Under COEP:credentialless, cross-origin
# IFRAMES (unlike subresources) are blocked unless they send their own COEP or
# carry the iframe `credentialless` attribute. The proper fix is to add that
# attribute to cross-origin app iframes in spawnIframeWindow (they then load, but
# credentialless = no cross-origin cookies, degrading auth'd apps like MoD). Left
# OFF pending that change + a decision on the auth tradeoff.
/apps/forge/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
/apps/anvil/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless

# Nothing embeds naklios.dev but naklios.dev itself (Immersive mode iframes the
# same-origin mirrors under /apps/<id>/). Without this, any site could frame the
# desktop (clickjacking of permission prompts and the git/AI credential forms)
# or frame a mirrored app and impersonate the host: the vendored SDK trusts the
# first parent origin that speaks `naklios:*`, so an attacker page answering
# `capabilities {fs:true}` would receive everything that app writes through
# naklios.fs. Found by the 2026-09-09 sweep; the deploy headers are the gate
# because a <meta> CSP cannot carry frame-ancestors.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# PWA manifest: the registered type, so every browser parses it as a manifest.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json

/apps/dish/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless

# Atelier's own Content-Security-Policy, copied from its repo's _headers (NakliTechie/atelier b4a9502).
# Cloudflare reads only this root file, so a mirrored apps/atelier/_headers would be ignored. Both
# this policy and the site-wide frame-ancestors 'self' apply, and the browser enforces each.
# connect-src * lets the AI features download models from Hugging Face and the CDN.
# 'unsafe-eval' is needed by the RAW decoder: libraw-wasm's Emscripten glue builds functions with new Function.
/apps/atelier/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' blob: data:; media-src 'self' blob: data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src * blob: data:; frame-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
/apps/atelier/vendor/tessella/vendor/libraw-wasm/libraw.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
